   blast5.tool_panic.written_to_terminal	thread 'tokio-rt-worker' (237374) panicked at src/main.rs:350:17:
   blast5.tool_panic.exit_code	0
   blast5.tool_panic.host_survived	true
   blast5.tool_panic.inner	inner.settle NONE — stream closed with no terminal event
   blast5.tool_panic.inner	inner.events Started,StepStarted,ModelCallCompleted,ToolProposed,ToolStarted
   blast5.tool_panic.inner	inner.outcome Err(operation interrupted: run task failed: task 9 panicked with message "LOOPRS_SPIKE_PANIC inside a rho-sdk tool call")
   blast5.tool_panic.inner	inner.retryable no
   	The panic is contained by the task the runtime spawned on, so the host
   	process lives — but the panic text goes to this process' stderr, which in
   	looprs is the user's terminal, mid-frame. That is the ADR-0006 hazard the
   	process boundary was also buying against.
