   	rho-sdk writes nothing: persistence is a value (`SessionSnapshot`, versioned
   	JSON) plus a host-implemented `SessionStore` trait, and `InMemorySessionStore`
   	is the only shipped impl. There is no session file, so there is nothing to opt
   	out of — which is the opposite of pi's session-file behaviour looprs' corpus
   	measurements currently depend on.
